cal record. Relevant to cause-and-effect analysis.", "newValue": "San Salvador de Jujuy, founded in 1593, serves as the capital of Jujuy Province in Argentina and is strategically located at the junction of the Andes and the valleys of the northwestern region of the country. Its establishment marked a pivotal moment in colonial Spanish expansion in South America, facilitating the consolidation of Spanish power and influence in the region, particularly during the Spanish colonial era. Prominent figures in its early history include local indigenous leaders and Spanish conquistadors, whose interactions shaped the social and political landscape of the area.

